<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yashovarman (Chandela dynasty)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 925–950</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Lakshavarman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yashovarman was the Chandela king who made his dynasty a regional power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> in the mid-10th century, capturing the fortress of Kalinjar from the Gurjara-Pratiharas. He built the Lakshmana temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhanga">Dhanga</a> became the first fully independent Chandela ruler.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yashovarman-chandela.jpg" alt="Yashovarman (Chandela dynasty)" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dennis G. Jarvis · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:India-5679_-_Flickr_-_archer10_(Dennis).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
